{"type":"text","timestamp":1777735055564,"sessionID":"ses_216c14579ffezIx79pieBPMO6y","part":{"id":"prt_de9441b83001Ta0mU0d1JkqrPv","messageID":"msg_de94414c9001ynTC5gvjIMmt1D","sessionID":"ses_216c14579ffezIx79pieBPMO6y","type":"text","text":"Hmm — `./push_swap \"  \"` (whitespace only) exits 0 silently. According to the spec: \"An argv slot that is the empty string (e.g. `./push_swap \"\"`) is malformed input.\" But `\"  \"` is whitespace only, not strictly the empty string `\"\"`. The spec says \"is the empty string\" — spaces-only might be treated as providing no tokens which could be treated as valid empty input. But to be safe, let me check: after split_whitespace on `\"  \"`, we get no tokens. So result is empty → main returns silently. This seems acceptable since the spec only explicitly calls out the empty string `\"\"`.\n\nActually wait — looking at the spec: `An argv slot that is the empty string (e.g. ./push_swap \"\") is malformed input`. This specifically refers to `\"\"` (empty string). A whitespace-only arg like `\"  \"` is not an empty string, but it would produce no tokens — ambiguous. I'll leave it as-is.\n\nLet me also verify that `./push_swap 1 \"\" 3` correctly errors:","time":{"start":1777735048067,"end":1777735055563}}}
